mode: "100644"
text: "# Workflows, checklists & worked examples\n\n## The daily short-form loop (repeatable)\nScript beats in → rough cut (kill dead air, hook first) → pace pass (change every ~2-4s, beat-sync) → caption\npass (auto + accuracy correction + saved style preset) → sound pass (license-checked) → spec export → WoopSocial.\nSave the caption style + intro/outro treatments as templates so the loop compresses to minutes.\n\n## The pre-edit tier check (avoids the export-paywall trap)\nBefore building the edit: are the effects/transitions/assets you plan to use on your tier? Is your export target\n(4K?) on your tier? Is the music from the commercial library and cleared for YOUR destination platform? Checking\nfor 2 minutes up front beats discovering at export that \"99% of the transitions were Pro-only\" (a documented\ncomplaint pattern — attribute).\n\n## The client-work hygiene checklist (the ToS gate)\nEditing client/NDA/confidential material? → local editing only ✓ · cloud sync/backup OFF for those projects ✓ ·\nno client assets in shared templates ✓ · client contract checked against platform-license terms ✓ · high-stakes →\ncounsel ✓ · or use a licensing-safe editor (Resolve/Premiere) for that work ✓.\n\n## Long-form routing\n>~15 min → not CapCut (by design). Talk-content long-form → Descript (text-based editing); cinematic/pro →\nResolve/Premiere. Then bring the master BACK for shorts: Long-Video-to-Shorts or captions-and-clipping /\nopus-clip for the cutdowns, CapCut for caption styling + pace.\n\n## Worked example A — \"Blunt indie founder\" (the retention edit)\n\"90 seconds of me rambling became 34 seconds that hold. cut the first 11 seconds (the warm-up nobody needed),\npunch-in every time i make a point, captions corrected — it wrote 'in voice' as 'invoice', which for once was\nright. music from the commercial library, checked it's cleared for more than tiktok. it wasn't. swapped it.\nexport, queue, done.\" — beats-first, accuracy pass, the license trap caught.\n\n## Worked example B — \"Warm bookkeeping studio\" (the caption preset)\n\"Captioning used to take us longer than filming — so we styled it once: our serif, cream on deep green, two lines,\ninside the safe zone, saved as a preset. Now every video is auto-caption → a careful read-through (it misspells\n'ledger' constantly, bless it) → apply the preset. One small step this week: build your preset once, and\ntomorrow-you gets twenty minutes back.\" — style once, reuse, the gentle accuracy pass.\n\n## Never\nShip uncorrected auto-captions · build the edit before checking asset tiers · assume \"Commercial use\" music is\ncleared beyond TikTok/CapCut · sync client/NDA material to the cloud · use pirated template packs or unlicensed\nsongs · lip-sync/deepfake a real person without consent · force long-form into a short-form tool · state a CapCut\nprice or feature gate as fact without verifying in-app · claim WoopSocial edits video.\n"
